---
/**
 * `/admin` used to render Editorial directly (T9.3, AdminHome). T1.6 (admin
 * latency plan): Editorial's `admin-editorial-view` call is the single
 * slowest call in the whole admin (16.0s cold / 9.8s warm — see
 * `editorial-view-client.ts`'s own header), so the very first thing a fresh
 * session painted was a 10-16s blank. Requests is the cheapest section
 * (5.6s, almost entirely the shell trio) and the surface with the "needs
 * you" pills — the one an operator actually wants first.
 *
 * Editorial moved to its own route, `/admin/editorial` (same AdminLayout +
 * AdminHome this file used to render — see that route file). This one is
 * now a redirect to `/admin/requests`, in the same static
 * meta-refresh-plus-canonical shape `/admin/maintenance` uses for its own
 * retirement redirect (`admin/maintenance.astro`), for the same reason:
 * `output: 'static'` (site-astro-config.ts) means there is no server at
 * request time to issue a real 3xx from an Astro page, so this is the
 * fallback the build can produce on its own. A `force=true` rule in
 * netlify.toml (the `/admin/maintenance`, `/admin/content`,
 * `/admin/templates`… precedent) would turn this into a true HTTP redirect
 * and would be a good, low-risk follow-up — out of scope here (T1.6's file
 * allow-list does not include netlify.toml).
 *
 * `shell-routes.ts` still registers `/admin` (required — it is a
 * bookmarked, typed-in-the-address-bar entry point) and
 * `admin-nav-route-parity.test.ts` lists it as intentionally unreached from
 * the sidebar, the same way it already does for `/admin/maintenance`.
 */
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/admin/requests" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="/admin/requests" />
    <title>Redirecting to Requests</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>Taking you to <a href="/admin/requests">Requests</a>.</p>
  </body>
</html>
